# Apache-side rules only.
#
# Cache policy is NOT here, deliberately. This server is Plesk running nginx in
# front of Apache with static-file processing on: nginx serves .html, .md and
# .pdf itself and never asks Apache, which is provable from the ETag formats --
# nginx writes "<hex-mtime>-<hex-size>" and Apache writes "<hex-size>-<hex-mtime>",
# and the homepage carries the nginx one. A Cache-Control directive in this file
# would therefore have no effect on the page that needs it while looking exactly
# like a fix. Cache policy lives in the nginx directives; see CACHING.md.
#
# What reaches Apache is PHP, and chat.php already sets its own no-store header.

# The key never belongs under the web root and chat.php refuses to read one from
# here. This is a backstop for the case where a key file is placed in httpdocs by
# mistake AND the request is handled by Apache rather than nginx. The matching
# nginx rule covers the other case; which layer answers for an unusual extension
# is not something worth guessing at, so both are set.
<FilesMatch "\.(key|pem|env)$">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>
